IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-succession-domain`
IMPORT `sg-isa`
IMPORT `sg-succession`

-- The corpus is Singapore law, so its clock is Singapore's. Declared even
-- though nothing below reads `RULES EFFECTIVE DATE` any more, because a
-- deployed module that ever gains a dated read should not fail at request time
-- with a timezone error.
TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `Singapore succession — the deployable façade`

-- ===========================================================================
-- THE DEPLOYABLE SURFACE.
--
-- The five corpus modules carry ZERO `@export` by design: they are inert, so a
-- domain expert can read them section by section against the Acts without
-- presentation concerns in the way. This module is the only exported one. It
--
--   (a) ROUTES flat, plain-English inputs into the corpus's own record types,
--   (b) CALLS the corpus's own predicates, and
--   (c) PRESENTS the answer as flat records a form can render and a JSON
--       client can read.
--
-- IT RE-IMPLEMENTS NO LAW. Every legal question below is delegated to
-- sg-isa.l4 / sg-wills.l4 / sg-paa.l4 through sg-succession.l4. If you find a
-- rule stated here, that is a defect: fix it by deleting it and calling the
-- corpus instead.
--
-- FIELD NAMES STAY UNDER 60 CHARACTERS. jl4-service sanitises schema property
-- names and TRUNCATES them at 60, so the corpus's own field names -- which are
-- the statutes' sentences -- would reach the wire amputated. Every name below
-- is short enough to survive intact.
--
-- WHAT THE FLAT SURFACE CANNOT SAY, and why that is recorded rather than
-- hidden: the corpus's `Person` is a TREE (ISA s 7 rule 3 distributes per
-- stirpes "to the remotest degree"), and a flat form cannot describe an
-- arbitrary family tree. This façade covers the shapes an ordinary enquiry
-- has -- counts per class, plus ONE level of representation for a predeceased
-- child. A deeper tree (a predeceased grandchild) needs the corpus API
-- directly, and `the family shape is fully described` says so rather than
-- quietly answering a different question.
-- ===========================================================================


§§ `Building the corpus's records from flat counts`

-- Distinct names are not attempted: L4 has no number-to-string, and the answer
-- a form needs is the SHARE PER CLASS, not per individual. Members of a class
-- therefore share a label, and a client that sums by taker gets the class's
-- total -- which is the number a person actually asks for ("what do the
-- children get between them?").
GIVEN howMany IS A NUMBER
      label   IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF Person
`the` howMany `survivors called` label MEANS
    replicate howMany (Person WITH `name`                  IS label
                                , `survived the deceased`  IS TRUE
                                , `issue`                  IS EMPTY)

-- ISA s 7 rule 3: a child who died before the deceased is represented by their
-- own children, who take that child's share between them.
GIVEN howManyStocks    IS A NUMBER
      childrenPerStock IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF Person
`the` howManyStocks `predeceased children each leaving` childrenPerStock MEANS
    replicate howManyStocks
      (Person WITH `name`                 IS "a grandchild"
                 , `survived the deceased` IS FALSE
                 , `issue`                 IS (`the` childrenPerStock `survivors called` "a grandchild"))


§§ `The question a person actually asks`

DECLARE `Succession answer`
    HAS `the law that applies`        IS A STRING
        `what to do next`             IS A STRING
        `the estate at death`         IS A NUMBER
        `left after debts and expenses` IS A NUMBER
        `divided by this Act`         IS A NUMBER
        `who takes, and how much`     IS A LIST OF Share
        `note`                        IS A STRING
        `the family shape is fully described` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The single entry point. Every argument is a fact a person can answer about
-- themselves without a lawyer; every answer comes from the corpus.
@export What happens to the estate when someone dies without a will
GIVEN `the deceased was Muslim`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased lived in Singapore`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `surviving spouses`                   IS A NUMBER
      `surviving children`                  IS A NUMBER
      `children who died first`             IS A NUMBER
      `children of each child who died`     IS A NUMBER
      `surviving parents`                   IS A NUMBER
      `surviving brothers and sisters`      IS A NUMBER
      `surviving grandparents`              IS A NUMBER
      `surviving uncles and aunts`          IS A NUMBER
      `value of the home in Singapore`      IS A NUMBER
      `value of everything else`            IS A NUMBER
      `debts, funeral and legal costs`      IS A NUMBER
      `year of death`                       IS A NUMBER
      `month of death`                      IS A NUMBER
      `day of death`                        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Succession answer`
`the succession answer` MEANS
    `Succession answer` WITH
        `the law that applies`          IS (`the Act governing the distribution in` theCase)
      , `what to do next`               IS (`what happens next in` theCase)
      , `the estate at death`           IS (`gross estate of` theCase)
      , `left after debts and expenses` IS (`distributable estate of` theCase)
      , `divided by this Act`           IS (`the property this Act distributes in` theCase)
      , `who takes, and how much`       IS (answer's `shares`)
      , `note`                          IS (answer's `note`)
      , `the family shape is fully described` IS shapeIsSimple
    WHERE
      answer  MEANS `the intestate distribution for` theCase
      -- One level of representation only; see the header note.
      shapeIsSimple MEANS `children who died first` EQUALS 0
                          OR `children of each child who died` GREATER THAN 0
      theCase MEANS
        Case WITH
            `deceased` IS (Deceased WITH `name` IS "the deceased"
                                    -- A FACT about the deceased, supplied by the
                                    -- caller. An earlier draft read `RULES
                                    -- EFFECTIVE DATE` here, which conflates the
                                    -- date the RULES are read at with the date the
                                    -- person DIED -- two different axes. ISA s 5
                                    -- turns on the latter.
                                    , `date of death` IS (YMD `year of death` `month of death` `day of death`)
                                    , `domiciled in Singapore` IS `the deceased lived in Singapore`
                                    , `Muslim` IS `the deceased was Muslim`)
          , `family` IS (Family WITH
                `surviving spouses` IS (`the` `surviving spouses` `survivors called` "the spouse")
              , `children`          IS (append (`the` `surviving children` `survivors called` "a child")
                                               (`the` `children who died first` `predeceased children each leaving` `children of each child who died`))
              , `parents`           IS (`the` `surviving parents` `survivors called` "a parent")
              , `siblings`          IS (`the` `surviving brothers and sisters` `survivors called` "a brother or sister")
              , `grandparents`      IS (`the` `surviving grandparents` `survivors called` "a grandparent")
              , `uncles and aunts`  IS (`the` `surviving uncles and aunts` `survivors called` "an uncle or aunt"))
          , `estate` IS (Estate WITH
                `immovable property in Singapore` IS `value of the home in Singapore`
              , `movable property in Singapore`   IS `value of everything else`
              , `funeral, testamentary and administration expenses` IS `debts, funeral and legal costs`
              , `debts and liabilities`           IS 0)
          , `will` IS NOTHING


§§ `A boolean decision, so the ladder and query-plan routes are reachable`

-- jl4-service's /ladder and /query-plan render a BOOLEAN decision's structure.
-- Without one exported, those two routes have nothing to answer for this
-- deployment. This asks the question a person asks first, and answers it from
-- the corpus's own s 2 / s 5 tests.
-- DOMICILE IS DELIBERATELY NOT A CONDITION HERE. Under ISA s 4(2) a Singapore
-- immovable is regulated by this Act "wherever he may have been domiciled", so
-- domicile changes WHAT the Act reaches, never WHETHER it decides. An earlier
-- draft carried a `the deceased lived in Singapore OR TRUE` conjunct, which is
-- a vacuous guard -- exactly what `l4 verify` exists to find, and not something
-- to ship in the same change as a linter about silent logic errors.
@export Does the Intestate Succession Act decide who inherits
GIVEN `the deceased was Muslim`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the deceased left a valid will` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act decides this estate` MEANS
    (NOT `the deceased was Muslim`) AND (NOT `the deceased left a valid will`)
